{
  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "**Optimize & Analyze Chat AI Backend Feature (apiamis)**\n\nConduct a comprehensive performance audit of the Chat AI feature in the apiamis backend, identify bottlenecks across the full request lifecycle, and implement prioritized optimizations covering latency, cost, reliability, and scalability.\n\n**Phase 1 — Current State Analysis**\n- Map full request flow: client → auth → prompt assembly → model inference → streaming → response persistence → logging\n- Profile baseline metrics: p50/p95/p99 latency, Time-to-First-Token (TTFT), total generation time, throughput (TPS), error rate, CPU/memory per session\n- Audit database schema: chat_history, message_vectors, session_metadata — check indexes, unbounded growth, N+1 queries, connection pool exhaustion\n- Document existing caching, rate limiting, retry mechanisms, and model configuration (model tier, temperature, max tokens)\n- Measure token usage per request and per session — identify waste from redundant system prompts, oversized histories, unnecessary context reprocessing\n\n**Phase 2 — Bottleneck Identification**\n- Break down time spent per layer: network I/O, DB reads/writes, AI service call, response serialization, streaming overhead\n- Evaluate streaming implementation: chunk size/interval, backpressure handling, connection reuse, disconnect recovery\n- Assess concurrency: queue management, HTTP keep-alive, async processing gaps, synchronous waits\n- Review prompt construction: sliding window vs. full history, truncation strategy, embedding reuse in RAG pipelines\n- Check for security gaps: prompt injection guards, input sanitization, output filtering\n\n**Phase 3 — Optimization Targets (Prioritized)**\n1. **Latency Reduction** — Prompt caching for frequent prefixes, context window trimming, streaming tuning, connection pooling\n2. **Cost Optimization** — Token budget tracking, model routing (cheap model for simple queries), response deduplication, conversation summarization for long histories\n3. **Database & Storage** — Add missing indexes (user_id, session_id, created_at), batch message writes, archive cold conversations, optimize vector retrieval if applicable\n4. **Concurrency & Scaling** — Async request queuing with backpressure, per-user/per-API-key rate limiting, burst handling with clear 429 responses\n5. **Reliability** — Idempotent retry with exponential backoff, circuit-breaker for model API failures, graceful degradation (fallback model or cached response), partial response recovery on disconnect\n6. **Observability** — Custom metrics (latency histograms, cache hit ratio, token consumption, error rates by type), structured logging, dashboard with alert thresholds\n\n**Phase 4 — Deliverables**\n- Baseline vs. optimized benchmark report (latency, throughput, token cost, error rate)\n- Prioritized recommendation matrix (Tier 1/2/3) with estimated effort and impact per item\n- Specific code/config changes (not just descriptions) for each recommendation\n- Monitoring dashboard config and recommended alert thresholds\n- Implementation roadmap for incremental rollout with A/B test checkpoints\n\n**Edge Cases to Investigate**\n- Long-running streaming sessions (disconnect handling, partial response recovery)\n- Concurrent multi-device access per user\n- Large message payloads / file attachments\n- Context window overflow (token limit exceeded mid-conversation)\n- Cost spikes from adversarial or excessively long prompts\n- Chat history migration / archival strategy at scale\n\n**Prerequisites**\n- Access to apiamis backend source code and deployment config\n- Database schema and query logs\n- Model provider usage dashboards, rate limits, and pricing details\n- Existing observability/APM stack (if any)\n- CI/CD pipeline for staging optimizations",
